From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:14:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 37/44] minimize: Firefox tab counts for blank windows and
 stale selections

Blank Firefox windows got no tab count: Firefox stores a blank tab's
URL (chrome://browser/content/blanktab.html) as its title, so the
session window never matched the window title "Mozilla Firefox".

A window that switched tabs since Firefox last wrote the session file
had no session window with its title as selected tab, so it got no
count. It now takes a session window whose selected tab no window
shows any more and whose pages include the window's title, when that
is the single best such window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

